# CHANGELOG.md grows by appending a section to the current release block, so
# two branches that each add one land their insertions on the same line and
# every concurrent lockstep PR conflicted there (five in a row on
# 2026-10-16). `union` keeps both sides in order, which is the resolution a
# human made each time. It only applies to local merges and rebases — GitHub's
# merge button does not read merge drivers — so the rule in CLAUDE.md is to
# rebase the next PR after each merge; with this, that rebase is
# conflict-free.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
